  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADEW workshop 2018-25</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADEW, established in 2005, is Australia&#x2019;s premier forum for discussing and disseminating research in the field of development economics. ADEW is a diverse group of individuals and institutions whose principle aim is to deepen knowledge about major development economics issues in the Asia-Pacific region, and to engage with the academic and policy communities with an interest in this area. 
ADEW consists of an annual two-day workshop that provides opportunities for senior and junior development economists from around the Asia-Pacific region, including DFAT staff, to present their work and engage with others.</narrative>
  </description>
